.SH TYPEDEFS
The following datatypes are defined in the dd.h header file.
.Ty
DD_CMTS_LEN
Maximum length of comments, 73 characters.

.Ty
DD_INSTR_LEN
Maximum length of the instrument keyword, 71 characters.

.Ty
DD_KEYWORD_LEN
Maximum length of a keyword, 9 characters.

.Ty
DD_VALUE_LEN
Maximum length of a value, 71 characters.

.Ty
DD_ROW
This structure contains all information about a row from the data dictionary.
oThe members of the structure are:
.Ss
char      ddrInstr[DD_INSTR_LEN];    /\(** Instrument name.      \(**/
char      *ddrAttrib;                /\(** Attribute name.       \(**/
char      ddrKeyword[DD_KEYWORD_LEN];/\(** Keyword name.         \(**/
DHS_DATA_TYPE
          ddrType;               /\(** Data type.            \(**/
int       ddrGemMand;                /\(** Gemini mandatory.     \(**/
char      ddrNullVal[DD_VALUE_LEN];  /\(** Null value.           \(**/
char      ddrArray;                  /\(** Array type.           \(**/
char      *ddrColName;               /\(** Column name.          \(**/
char      ddrCmts[DD_CMTS_LEN];      /\(** Comments.             \(**/
.Es

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dd
library provides management of the data dictionary.  The library has its own
configuration file which contains the data dictionary.

Following is a list of the library's functions:
.Ty
ddAttribGet()
This function searches for a row in its data dictionary given the 
.B instrument
and a FITS 
.B keyword 
name.  If a match is not found then an instrument wildcard of "*"
is used in the search.  If found, the row is returned
in the DD_ROW structure passed in.
.Ty
ddExit()
This function is used to cleanup and exit the data dictionary.
.Ty
ddGetNext()
This function returns a row from its data dictionary given the passed in
counter.  This allows you to cycle through each row in the data dictionary.
The list is sorted by the keyword and starts at 0.
The row from the data dictionary is returned in the DD_ROW structure
passed in, or NULL if the end of the list is reached.
.Ty
ddInit()
This function is used to initialize and read the data dictionary's 
configuration file.
.Ty
ddKeywordGet()
This function searches for a row in the data dictionary given the 
.B instrument
and an 
.B attribute 
name.  
If a match is not found then an instrument wildcard of "*"
is used in the search.  If found, the row is returned
in the DD_ROW structure passed in.


.SH FILES

.SS

The data dictionary library requires a configuration file called
.I libdd.config
which contains the data dictionary.

The data dictionary has ten columns.  The first one always has
the value "OK".  The remaining columns, starting at column two and
ending with column ten,  are as follows:

.LP
.PD 0
.TP 15
.I Instrument
The instrument used to acquire the data.  If the instrument is not
known then "*" is used.
.TP
.I Attribute
This is the attribute name used in the 
.B SDS 
structure.
.TP
.I Type
This is the data type and can be one of;
.B CHAR, STRING, BOOLEAN, BYTE,	UBYTE, SHORT, USHORT, INT, UINT,
.B FLOAT, DOUBLE,
or
.B ANY.  ANY
indicates that the data type could be of any type.
.TP
.I Keyword
This is the keyword that is found in or will be written in the 
.B FITS
file.
.TP
.I Gemini Mandatory
Has a value of either
.B T,
keyword is required in the primary header unit of a 
.B FITS
file, or
.B F,
keyword is not required in the primary header unit of a 
.B FITS
file.  This value is used by 
.B dhsData
to determine if this keyword should be found in the main header unit of a given
.B FITS
file.  For now it is best to use a value of F.
.TP
.I Null Value
This is used to check if the value in the 
.B FITS 
file is null.
.TP
.I Array Values
Indicates if the variable is multi-dimensional.  Valid values are
.B EXTEN,
a multi-dimensional array,
.B INDEX, an indexed array, or
.B NONE,
not an array.  Multi-dimensional arrays will be written to
.B FITS 
files as extension and indexed arrays become sequences of
keywords.
.TP
.I Column Name
Either 
.B NULL
or a 
.B column name.
This is used by 
.B dhsData 
to indicate the actual name of the column heading
in the database where, if the keyword is present in the 
.B FITS
file and not null,the data will be stored.  This column must exist in the
table used by the fh library (refer to the fh man page).
.TP
.I Comments
The comments to be written into the 
.B FITS 
file.

.PP
There are also a number of rules that must be adhered to in
the data dictionary.  They are as follows:

.IP 1. 
If the
.I Type 
is set to
.B ANY, 
then the 
.I Column Name 
must be set to "NULL"
.IP 2. 
If the
.If the
.I Type
is
.B ANY, 
then the
.I Null Value
must be set to "NULL"
.IP 3. 
If
.I Array Vaules
is not
.B NONE,
then the
.I Column Name
must be "NULL"
.IP 4.
The 
.I Instrument/Keyword
and
.I Instrument/Attribute 
pairs must be unique.
No two lines in the data dictionary can have the same values for the both
the 
.I Instrument 
and 
.I Keyword 
nor both the 
.I Instrument
and 
.I Attribute.
.IP 5.
.I Keyword 
values must be in upper-case to comply with 
.B FITS 
standards.
.IP 6.
If two rows have the same
.I Column Name
value then they must also have the same
.I Type.
.IP 7.
The table used by the 
.B dhsData
must exist with the columns listed in the
.I Column Name
values prior to starting

The following is an example of a portion of a configuration file.
(Text followed by a '#' is treated as a comment and ignored by
.B dd.

.sp
.nf

#
#  Data Dictionary
#  Instrument: An instrument name found in FITS, or the wildcard *
#  Attribute : The attribute name in an SDS structure.
#  Data Type: Valid values are:CHAR, STRING, BOOLEAN, BYTE, UBYTE, SHORT,
#     USHORT, INT, UINT, FLOAT, DOUBLE, or ANY which indicates not to check 
#     the data type as it can change.
#  Keyword: The keyword in the FITS file.
#  Gemini Mand.:  T or F.  This is for future use, set to F for now.
#  Null Value:  This is the value in the FITS or SDS struct that indicates it
#     is a null value.
#  Array: Valid values are: EXTEN, INDEX, NONE.  Which indicates if the
#     data is in a multi-dimensional array(EXTEN), an indexed array(INDEX),
#     or a scalar value(NONE).  Multi-dimensional arrays will be written in the
#     FITS file as FITS extensions, indexed arrays as a series of keywords, and
#     scalar values as a single keyword.
#  Column Name: Valid values are "NULL" (which indicates no column name), or a 
#     string name.  If it has a name, then when a FITS header is ingested, 
#     this keyword's value will be written to the database.
#  Comment: A quote enclosed comment.
#
#
#  Instrument	Attribute	Data	Keyword		 Gemini Mand.	Null	Array	Column	Comment	
#		Name in SDS	Type	Name in Fits	Keyword in Fits	Value		Name
#  ----------	---------	------	------------	-------------	-----	-----	-------	---------------------------------
#
OK FOC 		BSCALE   	DOUBLE 	BSCALE   	 	F	1.0	NONE	NULL	"REAL = TAPE*BSCALE + BZERO"
OK FOC 		BZERO    	DOUBLE 	BZERO    	 	F	0.0	NONE	NULL	""
OK FOC 		OBJECT   	STRING 	OBJECT   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Object ID"
OK FOC 		ORIGIN   	STRING	ORIGIN   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	""
OK FOC 		DATE     	STRING  DATE     	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	""
OK FOC 		IRAFNAME 	STRING	IRAFNAME 	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"NAME OF IRAF IMAGE FILE"
OK FOC 		IRAF-MAX 	FLOAT  	IRAF-MAX 	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"DATATA MAX"
OK FOC 		IRAF-MIN 	FLOAT  	IRAF-MIN 	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"DATA MIN"
OK FOC 		IRAF-BPX 	INT    	IRAF-BPX 	 	F	16	NONE	NULL	"DATA BITS/PIXEL"
OK FOC 		IRAFTYPE 	STRING  IRAFTYPE 	 	F	SHORT	NONE	NULL	"PIXEL TYPE"
OK FOC 		CRVAL1   	DOUBLE 	CRVAL1   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"RA at Ref pix in decimal degrees"
OK FOC 		CRVAL2   	DOUBLE 	CRVAL2   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL 	"DEC at Ref pix in decimal degrees"
OK FOC 		CRPIX1   	FLOAT  	CRPIX1   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Refpix of first axis"
OK FOC 		CRPIX2   	FLOAT  	CRPIX2   	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Refpix of second axis"
OK FOC	 	CD1_1    	FLOAT  	CD1_1    	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"CD matrix"
OK FOC 		CD1_2    	FLOAT  	CD1_2    	 	F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"CD matrix"
OK *		AXISSZ1      	INT	AXISSZ1    		F	3	NONE	NULL	"length of x axis for entire image"
OK *		AXISSZ2      	INT	AXISSZ2    		F	3	NONE	NULL	"lenght of y axis for entire image"
OK *		CHUNK		BOOLEAN	CHUNK   		F	3	NONE	NULL	"indicates if Fits file is a 'chunk' of data"
OK *		multiArray	ANY	ARRAY			F	NULL	EXTEN	NULL	"Multi-dimension array for testing."
OK *		EXTLEVEL	INT	EXTLEVEL		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"level of the extension file in a hierarchy"
OK PSPC		BLOCKED  	BOOLEAN	BLOCKED	 		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"FITS file may be blocked"
OK PSPC		BUNIT    	STRING	BUNIT   		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Units of data values"
OK PSPC		CDELT1 	 	DOUBLE	CDELT1	 		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Coordinate increment per pixel"
OK PSPC		CDELT2 	 	DOUBLE	CDELT2	 		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Coordinate increment per pixel"
OK NICMOS 	NBFCPYRT	INT	NBFCPYRT		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	"Number of brief copyright statement lines"
OK NICMOS	BFCPYRT1	STRING	BFCPYRT1		F	NULL	NONE	NULL	""
