.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

The environment variable
.B LIBDD_CONFIG_DIR may be set to the path of the 
directory containing the 
configuration file. If
.B LIBDD_CONFIG_DIR
is not set, 
.B DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR 
should be set to where the configuration file can be found.  If
that is not set then the current directory will be used.


